 ## Failure modes
 
 - **Shard-coverage drift**: if a repo structural test requires every `test-*.sh` to map to a Makefile target/shard, an invoke-only `test-trailer-awk.sh` could trip it. Earliest signal: `make test-harness-shards-coverage` (or the equivalent check) fails. Mitigation: the existing thin adapters are already invoke-only and pass, so follow that precedent; if the check is stricter than expected, register `test-trailer-awk` as its own target + shard entry instead.
 - **Awk dialect / Bash 3.2 portability**: macOS `awk` (BWK) vs gawk differences, or a Bash 4-only construct, could make the harness pass locally but fail in CI (or vice versa). Earliest signal: harness output differs across `awk` implementations. Mitigation: use only POSIX awk features the unit-under-test already relies on, and run `make lint-bash32` plus the harness locally.
-- **Over-pinning the regression guard**: an anchor string chosen too literally (e.g. a long sentence) could break on a benign reword of SKILL.md/approval-gates.md. Earliest signal: `test-design-structure.sh` fails after an unrelated doc edit. Mitigation: pin short, stable tokens (`--snapshot-trailers`, `--dedup`, `gate-b-dedup-plan.sh`), not full sentences.
+- **`set -e` abort on expected `has_key` failure**: invoking exit-1 probes bare under `set -euo pipefail` aborts before assertions run. Earliest signal: harness exits on the first absent-key case with no `FAIL:` label. Mitigation: wrap every expected non-zero awk/`has_key` probe in `set +e` … `set -e` (or `if ! awk …`); document the pattern in `test-trailer-awk.md`.
+- **Over-pinning the regression guard**: duplicating (3175) `$SKILL_MD` pins or choosing overly literal anchor strings could break on benign doc edits. Earliest signal: `test-design-structure.sh` fails after an unrelated edit. Mitigation: extend the existing block only; tighten weak `snapshot` substrings to literal `--snapshot-trailers` / `--dedup`; do not re-add SKILL tokens already covered at 397–402.
 
